// @trap memory access out of bounds
// THE BOUNDS POLICY through the narrowest write there is. VL adds no check of its
// own; the engine's is the policy (§A4), and it traps loudly.
//
// This is the cell the `std:buffer` read-modify-write emulation had to imitate and
// could only ALMOST: `poke8` reached the byte at 65536 through the WORD at 65536,
// and argued its way to the same trap because a memory's size is a multiple of 4.
// The instruction needs no argument — a single-byte store one byte past the one
// page the module starts with is out of bounds, and that is the whole proof.
//
// `store-narrow-widths-round-trip.vl` writes the last LEGAL byte at 65535 among its
// in-bounds cells; this is the one byte further.
__store_i8__(65536, 1)
print(1)
